NNAAMMEE
       anytopnm - convert an arbitrary type of image file to PBM, PGM, or PPM


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       aannyyttooppnnmm [_f_i_l_e]



DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       aannyyttooppnnmm  converts  the  input  image, which may be in any of about 100
       graphics formats, to PBM, PGM, or PPM format, depending on that  nature
       of the input image, and outputs it to Standard Output.

       To  determine  the  format of the input, aannyyttooppnnmm uses the ffiillee program
       (possibly assisted by the magic numbers  file  fragment  included  with
       Netpbm).  If  that  fails  (very few image formats have magic numbers),
       aannyyttooppnnmm looks at the filename  extension.   If  that  fails,  aannyyttooppnnmm
       punts.

       The type of the output file depends on the input image.

       aannyyttooppnnmm  uses  the converters for particular graphics formats that are
       in the Netpbm package, so it can't convert any format that you couldn't
       convert  with  some  other  Netpbm  program.  What aannyyttooppnnmm adds is the
       ability to recognize the format and choose the appropriate Netpbm  pro‐
       gram to convert it.  For example, if you invoke aannyyttooppnnmm on a GIF file,
       aannyyttooppnnmm will recognize that it is a GIF file  and  therefore  ggiiffttooppnnmm
       knows how to convert it to PNM, so aannyyttooppnnmm invokes ggiiffttooppnnmm.

       aannyyttooppnnmm cannot recognize every possible input format, so you may still
       be able to convert an image with a specific Netpbm  program  when  aannyy‐‐
       ttooppnnmm fails to convert it.

       If  ffiillee  indicates  that the input file is compressed (either via Unix
       compress, gzip, or bzip compression), aannyyttooppnnmm uncompresses it and pro‐
       ceeds as above with the uncompressed result.

       If  ffiillee  indicates that the input file is encoded by uuencode or btoa,
       aannyyttooppnnmm decodes it and proceeds as above with the decoded result.

       If _f_i_l_e is -- or not given, aannyyttooppnnmm takes its input from  Standard  In‐
       put.

       Many  image  formats  are  capable of representing multiple images.  In
       most cases, aannyyttooppnnmm converts these to multi-image Netpbm  images,  but
       for  some  formats,  aannyyttooppnnmm converts only the first image and ignores
       the rest.

       In the case of a multi-image GIF input, aannyyttooppnnmm converts all  the  im‐
       ages  starting with Netpbm 10.69 (December 2014), but only the first in
       earlier releases.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       There are no command line options defined specifically for aannyyttooppnnmm.

       aannyyttooppnnmm does not recognize the options common to all programs based on
       libnetpbm (See
        Common  Options  ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩  .)  However, the --vveerrssiioonn
       option works.


